================================================================================
## Graph Chat port follow-up: Explorer search default 50 and tool spans
================================================================================

Context:
A line-by-line check of the 0.8.1-line Graph Chat performance work
(feat/graph-chat-performance 8387f8a3) against this port found two items lost
while resolving conflicts with 0.9.0: the Explorer graph-search default of 50
entities (with 50 / 100 / 200 choices) had reverted to 0.9.0's 5,000, and Graph
Chat tool calls no longer opened an MLflow TOOL span each.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/explorer/GraphFilter.py
   EXPLORER_MAX_ENTITIES_MIN 100 -> 50 and EXPLORER_MAX_ENTITIES_DEFAULT
   5000 -> 50 (the minimum). The 20,000 UI ceiling is unchanged.
2. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sigmagraph.html
   #sgMaxEntities gains 50 (selected), 100 and 200; 5 000 is no longer the
   selected option.
3. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   DEFAULT_MAX_ENTITIES fallback 5000 -> 50 to match the backend default.
4. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   New _dispatch_chat_tool, decorated with @trace_tool(), wraps the shared
   dispatch_tool, so each Graph Chat tool call shows as a `tool:<name>` span
   with its ok/error status. Following 0.9.0 (agent_owl_generator.staged), the
   span is per agent: decorating engine_base.dispatch_tool itself would
   double the owl generator's spans and change every other agent's traces.
5. tests/units/agents/test_agent_tracing.py,
   tests/units/dtwin/test_filter_expand.py,
   tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py
   Tests for the Graph Chat tool span, the new lower clamp, the dropdown minimum
   and the script fallback matching the backend default.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/explorer/GraphFilter.py
- src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sigmagraph.html
- src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
- src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
- tests/units/agents/test_agent_tracing.py
- tests/units/dtwin/test_filter_expand.py
- tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-20.log

Tests: tests/units 9091 passed, 12 skipped, 1 xfailed, 0 failed (deselected the
live-warehouse readiness test, which hangs locally on plain 0.9.0 too).

================================================================================
## Explorer expand keeps the searched entities when the cap is hit
================================================================================

Context:
Searching one customer at depth 2 with a 50-entity cap returned a hub
(the customer's country) and other customers of that country, but not the
searched customer: the single-statement expand capped the union of all BFS
levels with a bare LIMIT, so Postgres kept an arbitrary subset and could
drop the seeds and their direct neighbours. Present in plain 0.9.0.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/adjacency.py
   New ranked_entity_ctes(): the capped entity set is ordered by the
   nearest BFS level (then entity), so seeds come first, then level 1, and
   so on. expand_and_fetch_sql uses it.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   The Delta expand path uses the same helper instead of its own copy of
   the unordered CTEs.
3. tests/units/graphdb/test_adjacency_sql.py
   SQL-shape test for the hop ordering, plus a SQLite run of a seed -> hub
   -> 100 leaves graph capped at 5 that must keep seed and hub.
4. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Ratcheted: DeltaFlatStore.expand_and_fetch_subgraph is back under the
   function budget; other entries shrank.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/graphdb/adjacency.py
- src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
- tests/units/graphdb/test_adjacency_sql.py
- tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-20.log

